<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Hastie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1786–1826</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Hastie was a British agent at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radama-i">Radama I</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> from 1817 until his death in 1826. Sent by Robert Farquhar, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritius">Mauritius</a>, he negotiated the Anglo-Merina treaties of 1817 and 1820 that ended the export of slaves in return for arms, training and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subsidy">subsidies</a>. He helped Radama build a European-drilled army and opened the way for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society">London Missionary Society</a>.</p></div>
